  "solution": {
    "text": "For urea <math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>NH</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>CONH</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> </mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> </math> the van't Hoff factor can not be greater than unity because urea is non-ionisable while other are ionic compounds so will undergo dissociate in aqueous solution so&nbsp;van't Hoff factor will become more then unity."
